name sloane-electrical-dictionary
# The Standard Electrical Dictionary (Sloane, 1892). An entry is a term on a line of its own, then its definition and
# the book's references. What an entry attests of its term: the terms it refers to ("See X", "(see X)") and the synonyms
# its foot lists ("Synonyms--A--B."). Its definition is the entry's content, a usage of the term, not a claim.
match standard-electrical-dictionary-sloane.txt
format sloane

thing entry term
# A reference is "See"/"see" and the term it names: parted so that only the name is said.
part crossref by | is space
content term qualifier text other synonym See see
value - synonym See see
attest entry synonym crossref
